From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winewayland: Preserve the window cursor across surface recreation.

The native tray menu path recreates its Wayland surface when a hidden menu
is shown again. The Win32 HWND remains alive, but its cached HCURSOR was
stored on the destroyed surface. Pointer entry then treats the new surface's
zero-initialized cursor as an instruction to hide the pointer.

The server only sends WM_WINE_SETCURSOR when the cursor window or cursor
handle changes. A replacement surface is not such a change, so another
SetCursor call with the same handle need not repair the lost cursor. Updates
received while a window has no Wayland surface were also discarded.

Keep the last driver cursor in wayland_win_data, including explicit NULL
updates, so it follows the HWND lifetime instead of the surface lifetime.
This preserves intentional cursor hiding, including overlay suppression;
do not substitute an arrow cursor for NULL.

Acquire the pointer mutex before reading or updating the cached cursor,
using the existing win_data -> pointer lock order. Otherwise a pointer-enter
callback can read an old cursor, release win_data, and apply it after another
thread has already installed a newer cursor. Release win_data before the
GDI and protocol calls, and reapply clipping after releasing the pointer lock.

Extends Alexandros Frantzis's upstream per-window cursor tracking from
fe1f3e277d25b299c8c526c3d706a38fbde24e11. The native SNI menu support is
based on Erhan Bilgili (nanomatters)'s work in wine-wineland.

Related: https://github.com/GloriousEggroll/proton-ge-custom/issues/803#issuecomment-5881174211
---
diff --git a/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_pointer.c b/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_pointer.c
--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_pointer.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_pointer.c
@@ -931,30 +931,25 @@
 static void wayland_set_cursor(HWND hwnd, HCURSOR hcursor, BOOL use_hcursor)
 {
     struct wayland_pointer *pointer = &process_wayland.pointer;
-    struct wayland_surface *surface;
     struct wayland_win_data *data;
-    double scale;
+    double scale = 1.0;
     BOOL reapply_clip = FALSE;
 
-    if ((data = wayland_win_data_get(hwnd)))
+    /* Serialize the cached cursor and its application, in win_data -> pointer
+     * lock order, so an enter cannot overwrite a concurrent SetCursor update. */
+    data = wayland_win_data_get(hwnd);
+    pthread_mutex_lock(&pointer->mutex);
+    if (data)
     {
-        if (!(surface = data->wayland_surface))
-        {
-            wayland_win_data_release(data);
-            return;
-        }
-        scale = surface->window.scale;
-        if (use_hcursor) surface->hcursor = hcursor;
-        else hcursor = surface->hcursor;
+        /* A hidden window may have no surface yet. Keep its cursor anyway:
+         * the server need not resend an unchanged cursor when it is shown. */
+        if (use_hcursor) data->hcursor = hcursor;
+        else hcursor = data->hcursor;
         use_hcursor = TRUE;
+        if (data->wayland_surface) scale = data->wayland_surface->window.scale;
         wayland_win_data_release(data);
     }
-    else
-    {
-        scale = 1.0;
-    }
 
-    pthread_mutex_lock(&pointer->mutex);
     if (pointer->focused_hwnd == hwnd)
     {
         if ((!use_hcursor && pointer->wp_cursor_shape_device_v1) ||
diff --git a/dlls/winewayland.drv/waylanddrv.h b/dlls/winewayland.drv/waylanddrv.h
--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/waylanddrv.h
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/waylanddrv.h
@@ -553,7 +553,6 @@
     RECT geometry;
     int content_width, content_height;
     UINT32 alpha_multiplier;
-    HCURSOR hcursor;
 };
 
 BOOL wayland_dmabuf_format_supported(uint32_t format, uint64_t modifier);
@@ -681,6 +680,8 @@
     struct rb_entry entry;
     /* hwnd that this private data belongs to */
     HWND hwnd;
+    /* last driver cursor, including NULL, survives Wayland surface recreation */
+    HCURSOR hcursor;
     /* last buffer that was set as window contents */
     struct wayland_shm_buffer *window_contents;
     /* whether GDI pixels need to be composited above accelerated content */
